Algorithm
1. Start the NS-3 simulation and read the routing protocol, network condition, and output CSV filename.
2. Create two source nodes, three router nodes, and two destination nodes.
3. Install the selected routing protocol: RIP, AODV, or Global Routing.
4. Connect the nodes using CSMA links and assign IP addresses.
5. Install UDP packet sinks at the destination nodes.
6. Generate UDP traffic from the source nodes at 1 Mbps.
7. If congestion is selected, add extra UDP traffic at 9 Mbps.
8. If failure is selected, schedule the Router 0–Router 1 link to be disabled at 10 seconds.
9. Run the simulation for 31 seconds and collect statistics using FlowMonitor.
10. Calculate throughput, packet loss, packet delivery ratio, transmission ratio, and end-to-end delay.
11. Display the results and save them to a CSV file.
12. Stop the simulation and end.
